  "title": "Kerala's Name Change Bill and Railways' Dispute",
  "summary": "The Kerala Name Change Bill aims to rename the state to Keralam, with the Lok and Rajya Sabha passing the bill on August 11, 2026, following approval in 2024. Meanwhile, the Railway Board's decision to detach Mangaluru from the Palakkad division caused losses for Southern Railway and Keralam, with CM Satheesan seeking public input.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Lok and Rajya Sabha passed the Kerala (Alteration of Name) Bill, 2026, on August 11, 2026.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Railway Board's August 21 order to detach Mangaluru from Palakkad caused losses for Southern Railway and Keralam.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Chief Minister, V.D. Satheesan, seeks public input to reverse the new order.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
